{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-spectral-sequence-collapse","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:spectral-sequence-collapse","kind":"proposition","title":"Limit page of the GB spectral sequence for semisimple $H_n(R, q)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-gb-spectral-sequence"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.WedderburnMass.centralIdempotent_idem","text":"spectral-sequence-collapse.md","leanSource":"spectral-sequence-collapse.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:spectral-sequence-collapse\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a field and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in R</code> such that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = H_n(R, q)</code> is semisimple and separable over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>. Then Hochschild cohomology vanishes in positive degrees, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{HH}^k(A,\\, A) = 0</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k \\geq 1</code>. Hence the limit page of the GB filtration spectral sequence is concentrated in total degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_\\infty^{0,0} = \\mathrm{HH}^0(A, A) = Z(A)</code>.</em></p>\n<p><em>This does not say the sequence collapses at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_1</code>: a zero abutment in positive degree is compatible with non-zero <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_1</code> terms that are cancelled by differentials.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/spectral-sequence-collapse.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"11.1.29","page":"b/prop-spectral-sequence-collapse","qa":{"counts":{"pass":88,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":75},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
